0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 281.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 285.00 Td (Q1: What is the core objective of your project?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 270.80 Td (A: Our project implements MUREN \(CVPR 2023\) for Human-Object Interaction \(HOI\) detection. It detects humans and objects using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 259.30 Td (bounding boxes and predicts their interactive action as <Subject, Verb, Object> triplets.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 237.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 241.00 Td (Q2: How is HOI detection different from standard Object Detection?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 226.80 Td (A: Object detection only identifies object classes and their locations \('what' and 'where'\). HOI detection goes one level deeper) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 215.30 Td (to identify the semantic relationship and activity between the human and object \('what action is occurring'\).) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 193.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 197.00 Td (Q3: What does MUREN stand for?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 182.80 Td (A: MUREN stands for MUltiplex RElation Network. It models unary, pairwise, and ternary relations across human, object, and action) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 171.30 Td (queries.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 149.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 153.00 Td (Q4: Why did you choose a Transformer-based architecture over CNNs?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 138.80 Td (A: CNNs have localized receptive fields and struggle to connect humans and distant objects. Transformers use self-attention to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 127.30 Td (capture global contextual relationships across the entire image in a single pass.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 105.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 109.00 Td (Q5: What are the three branches in the MUREN decoder?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 94.80 Td (A: The three parallel branches are: \(1\) Human Branch \(predicts human bounding box\), \(2\) Object Branch \(predicts object bounding) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 83.30 Td (box and class\), and \(3\) Relation Branch \(predicts the verb/action\).) Tj ET

