0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 744.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 748.00 Td (Q6: What is the function of the MURE module?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 733.80 Td (A: MURE \(Multiplex Relation Encoder\) enables cross-talk between the three decoder branches. It computes ternary representations,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 722.30 Td (unary self-attentions, and pairwise cross-attentions to form a comprehensive multiplex relational context.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 700.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 704.00 Td (Q7: What is the ATF module?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 689.80 Td (A: ATF \(Attention-based Task Fusion\) dynamically injects the MURE relational context back into each individual branch using a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 678.30 Td (Sigmoid-gated adaptive fusion layer.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 656.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 660.00 Td (Q8: Which datasets did you use and what are their specifications?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 645.80 Td (A: Primary dataset is HICO-DET with 47,776 images, 80 object classes, 117 action verbs, and 600 HOI categories. Secondary dataset) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 634.30 Td (is V-COCO with 10,346 images, 81 objects, and 29 action classes.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 612.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 616.00 Td (Q9: What loss functions are used to train the model?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 601.80 Td (A: A combination of: \(1\) Focal Loss for verb classification \(tackles class imbalance\), \(2\) Cross-Entropy for object) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 590.30 Td (classification, \(3\) L1 Loss for bounding box coordinates, and \(4\) GIoU Loss for spatial box overlap.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 568.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 572.00 Td (Q10: How does the Hungarian Matcher work?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 557.80 Td (A: Since the model predicts 64 fixed queries while images have varying ground truths, the Hungarian algorithm finds a global) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 546.30 Td (minimum-cost bipartite matching between predicted queries and ground truth annotations.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 524.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 528.00 Td (Q11: What benchmark performance does MUREN achieve?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 513.80 Td (A: On the HICO-DET test set, MUREN achieves 32.87 mAP under the default setting and 35.52 mAP under the Known Object setting,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 502.30 Td (outperforming older models like QPIC and CDN.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 480.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 484.00 Td (Q12: Why does the relation branch use Sigmoid activation instead of Softmax?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 469.80 Td (A: Because a person can perform multiple actions with the same object simultaneously \(multi-label classification, e.g. holding and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 458.30 Td (inspecting\). Softmax assumes mutually exclusive single labels, whereas Sigmoid treats each verb independently.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 436.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 440.00 Td (Q13: How does your web application handle video tracking?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 425.80 Td (A: It samples frames at regular intervals, runs MUREN inference on each frame, and tracks human-object pairs over time using an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 414.30 Td (IoU spatial overlap matching threshold to construct continuous Action Intervals.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 392.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 396.00 Td (Q14: What is the latency and can it run on CPU?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 381.80 Td (A: Yes! Inference on CPU takes approximately 600ms - 1200ms per image. On an NVIDIA GPU \(e.g. RTX 3060/4060\), latency drops to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 370.30 Td (~40ms - 60ms, enabling real-time video processing.) Tj ET
1.00 w
0.940 0.960 0.990 rg 36.00 348.00 523.28 17.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.080 0.220 0.480 rg 42.00 352.00 Td (Q15: What are the main limitations and future scopes of this project?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 337.80 Td (A: Limitations: \(1\) Limited to 80 COCO objects and 117 verbs; \(2\) Performance drops in heavily occluded or crowded scenes. Future) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.180 0.220 0.280 rg 46.00 326.30 Td (scope: Integrating Vision-Language models like CLIP for open-vocabulary zero-shot HOI detection.) Tj ET
